                                                              6               Could a Great Coach Boost Your Country’s Medal Count?
                                                                                                                    M



                                                                  In competitive sports, achieving success depends not only on the skills and training of athletes
                                                                                                        ：




                                                              but also significantly on the influence of coaches. The term "great coach" refers to those who
                                                              achieve remarkable achievements with various teams or countries due to their outstanding tactical
                                                                                                       号




                                                              knowledge, extensive expertise, and ability to inspire their teams. These coaches are not limited
                                                              by their nationality; they can transcend borders, sharing their coaching experience and strategies in
                                                                                            信




                                                              diverse sports environments, which can enhance the overall performance of their teams. However, this
                                                              is merely a perception. Is the "great coach" effect genuinely real? In the following discussion, we will
                                                                                           微




                                                              explore the existence of the "great coach" effect and attempt to assess its impact on the medal tallies
                                                              of different nations.
                                                                            To examine the "Great Coach" phenomenon, we initially selected four prominent coaches:

                                                                            1. Lang Ping, who led the U.S. women’s volleyball team to a silver medal at the 2008 Beijing
                                                                               Olympics and guided the Chinese women’s volleyball team to a gold medal at the 2016 Rio
