       (c) The output of association rules is typically presented in the form of "if... then...", making
           the interpretation of the rules intuitive and easy to understand.
       (d) GRI can discover multi-level associations. For example, it can reveal not only the relation-
           ship between a single event and the total number of medals but also the combined impact
           of multiple events on the number of medals.

  3. Mixed-effects Model. Mixed-effects models are highly effective for assessing significant differ-
     ences among various levels of factors and accurately estimating the effects associated with fixed
     factor levels. This model facilitates the investigation of the "great coach" effect, showcasing




                                                           型
     both efficacy and clarity in their application.




